<title>JAPAN: MIKUNI ASSIGNS PRELIMINARY BOND CREDIT RATINGS.</title>
<headline>MIKUNI ASSIGNS PRELIMINARY BOND CREDIT RATINGS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Art Life Co Ltd, 480.32 million yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>East Japan Railway Company</p>
<p>40 billion yen mortgaged due 2009.</p>
<p>30 billion yen mortgaged due 2017.</p>
<p>Mr Max Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured euroyen convertible due 2001, private placement.  </p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Nippon Paint Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>Oki Electric Industry Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>Rengo Co Ltd,</p>
<p>five billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>five billion yen unsecured due 2007.</p>
<p>SXL Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Nichirei Corp, 20 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>Nippon Light Metal Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
<p>Sumitomo Special Metals Co Ltd, 15 billion yen unsecured euroyen convertible due 2004.</p>
<p>Nichiro Corp, five billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
</text>
